    <summary>Offline editor for legacy binary Word 97-2003 .doc files, with text, font and bookmark editing.</summary>
    <description><![CDATA[Nebula Doc is an offline Windows desktop editor for legacy binary Microsoft Word 97-2003 `.doc` files. Microsoft Word is not required.

## Features

- Open existing binary `.doc` files and save real Word 97-2003 `.doc` files.
- Edit body text and text inside existing table cells, including shaded cells.
- Change font family, size, bold, italic, underline and text colour.
- Navigate, create, rename and delete bookmarks.
- Undo and redo, zoom, bookmark search, Save and Save a copy.
- A `.doc.bak` copy is made before the first overwrite of an existing file.
- No accounts, uploads, telemetry or cloud services. Documents are processed locally.

## Notes

- Requires Windows 10 or 11 x64.
- Documents are processed by a private LibreOffice runtime bundled with the application. It does not install LibreOffice system-wide and does not affect an existing LibreOffice installation. LibreOffice is distributed under the Mozilla Public License 2.0; its licence and notices are installed with the application.
- `.docx`, RTF, encrypted documents and Word versions earlier than Word 97 are not supported.
- This is a focused editor, not a complete Word replacement. Headers, footers, fields, drawings and page settings are preserved but are not editable, and the editing view does not reproduce Word's pagination.
- The installer is approximately 290 MB because it includes the LibreOffice runtime.
- The installed executable is `nebula-doc.exe`. This package installs for all users and requires administrator rights. The installer is unsigned.

Nebula Doc is not affiliated with or endorsed by Microsoft or The Document Foundation.]]></description>
    <releaseNotes>https://github.com/Porkstone/nebula-doc/releases/tag/v1.0.1</releaseNotes>
